Think: Generate shell test commands from each line of temp_file_sizes.txt using awk (extracting the last field as size and the rest as path), execute them to verify existence and actual size, and write valid unique entries to ready_for_summation.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  size=$NF;
  path=substr($0,1,length($0)-length(size)-1);
  gsub(/"/, "\\\"", path);
  printf "path=\"%s\"; size=%s; if [ -f \"$path\" ]; then actual=$(stat -c %%s \"$path\"); if [ \"$actual\" -eq $size ]; then printf \"%s %s\\n\" \"$path\" \"$size\"; fi; fi\n", path, size
}' temp_file_sizes.txt | bash | awk '!seen[$0]++ {print}' > ready_for_summation.txt
```

